  "data": {
    "A": "Research asymptotic improvements in src/est_matriz_seq.c. Replace per-column bubble sort with stable O(R log R) mergesort using reusable scratch storage, and replace quadratic mode counting with an O(R) equality-run scan wherever equivalence is established. Measure sort-only, mode-only and combined variants. For ordinary finite inputs, retain the first sorted value among tied maximal frequencies and return -1 when nothing repeats. Audit both float variables, conta and moda, rather than silently increasing their precision. Preserve signed-zero ordering and provide a comparison-compatible general path for exceptional doubles; ordinary total-order sorting is not necessarily equivalent to bubble sort around NaNs. Keep mean/harmonic accumulation before sorting and variance accumulation in sorted order. Do not reproduce uninitialized-memory behavior; flag any unresolved oracle conflict.",
    "B": "Research serial input and memory-traffic improvements independently of A. Compare existing fscanf with buffered tokenization plus strtod, preserving valid floating-point syntax and tokens spanning buffer boundaries; do not assume integer inputs or restricted decimal precision. Test fusing arithmetic and reciprocal sums into one original-order traversal, or accumulating them during input while retaining each column's exact operation sequence. Retain the column-major representation unless measurements justify an additional transpose. Reduce redundant passes and allocation overhead without replacing sorted-order variance by an unsorted or sum-of-squares formula. Preserve printf rounding, metric ordering, trailing spaces and newlines. Evaluate parsing and scan changes separately so G can integrate only useful components.",
    "C": "Research coarse-grained parallelism on the four ARM64 CPU cores, using only facilities supported by the unchanged build. Partition independent columns among at most four workers, with disjoint results and private sorting scratch; keep output serial and ordered. Preserve sequential floating-point accumulation within every column—no parallel reductions or reassociation. Compare one, two and four workers where supported, including creation and synchronization costs. Develop a general workload-size cutoff that retains serial execution for small or narrow matrices, not a dispatch keyed to test identities or values. If threading requires forbidden build changes, pursue serial locality or vectorization across independent columns instead. Report when overhead outweighs gains.",
    "G": "Integrate only programs produced by A/B/C that pass the unchanged correctness checks and have a defensible general-input correctness argument. Start with the best measured standalone candidate, then measure selective combinations and ablations; parser, allocation, sorting and threading changes can interact adversely. Retain the fastest valid measured version, including a standalone version if integration regresses. Use the existing timing procedure and budget, treating small differences cautiously at this baseline duration. Review odd/even row counts, single-row variance, tied and absent modes, float mode conversion, zero/negative values, signed zero, exceptional values and rounding boundaries without changing tests or oracle. Preserve all seven output lines exactly. Reject unresolved semantic changes; never exploit mode's uninitialized storage, hardcode answers, or modify compiler, target, permissions or budgets.",
    "analysis": "The relevant task is Problem B, Descriptive Statistics Metrics. With R rows and K columns, both bubble sorting and mode counting cost O(KR²); the remaining statistical traversals are linear, and columns already occupy contiguous storage. These quadratic routines are the strongest source-based optimization candidates, but no hotspot measurements are supplied. The only measured program is the valid baseline: mean 0.009319 seconds, three samples approximately 0.009166–0.009421 seconds, and four correctness cases. This short duration makes parsing, startup and parallel overhead important, without establishing their actual shares. The target is four-core ARM64 without GPUs. Correctness depends on original-order arithmetic/harmonic sums, sorted-order variance and exact one-decimal output formatting. A significant reference defect is that moda_aux increments uninitialized cont[i]; it also narrows mode values and running maxima to float. Baseline acceptance neither defines that uninitialized behavior nor establishes correctness for every valid input. Optimization must not exploit it."
